boot [meas: CtrlTest boot]: loader 23 words + hello 36 code + 2 data words = 31 mode-5 packets and 2 mailbox packets from C&C; all 64 READY at cycle 71, RUN raised at 71, every tile at main's ebreak by 150
registers [meas: CtrlTest registers]: write-only reads 0; counters 20 bits; HIST 17, PTR 20, STREAM/GROUP 64 bits through the window; send port modes 2, 5, 6, 7 to the tile itself with auto-increment +2/+1 and SET_HI cleared per send; local wake after each; status and done readable the next cycle
command phases [meas: CtrlTest commands]: per GO, all-READY -> GO store (C&C) and READY round trip
  GO 0: all READY at 264, GO stored at 265, seen by tiles at 266-267
  GO 1: all READY at 307, GO stored at 308, seen by tiles at 309-310
  GO 2: all READY at 349, GO stored at 350, seen by tiles at 351-352
  GO 3: all READY at 391, GO stored at 392, seen by tiles at 393-394
  GO 4: all READY at 952, GO stored at 953, seen by tiles at 954-955
  two-command phase: start store 25 cycles after GO on every tile; local copy of 512 records, start -> READY 533 cycles
  the next command, sent right after GO: its first mailbox write lands 6 cycles after the tile saw GO at the earliest (tile 0), into the other argument block;
  its slot 0 (zero-argument commands) 6 cycles after GO at the earliest, after the woken tile read the previous command word (the simulator checks every slot-0 landing)
WFI [meas: CtrlTest wfi]: latch before WFI falls through in 1 cycle; a counter store clears the latch; a count of 0 makes no edge; GO is not latched; READY fires at done when the command landed first; uncounted packets made 256 local-wake edges that the qualifier (DEV) kept from waking
faults [meas: CtrlTest faults]: store to MASTER_STATUS, load from instruction memory, sub-word register store, the table window's gap and a misaligned load are bus errors; div and a CSR read are illegal; ecall halts; each cause logged, its condition set, no READY; HALT clears the conditions and HALT -> RUN restarts every core at the loader
invariants [meas: CtrlTest invariants]: 4 (done before arrivals), 5 (a mode-0 packet sent), 7 (packet in flight at a line change), 8 (reply overwritten unread), 9 (unexpected arrival: its condition set; a store to the reserved MASTER_PULSE[3] ignored and flagged; M14) and the table-window check each fire on a bad program
